Article 12 The State shall support the following projects for the transformation of scientific and technological achievements through government procurement, research and development subsidies, publication of industrial technology guidance catalogues, demonstration and promotion, among others:
(1) those that can significantly improve industrial technology level and economic benefits, or can form new industries that promote the healthy development of social economy;
(2) those that can significantly improve national security capabilities and public safety levels;
(3) those that can rationally develop and utilize resources, save energy, reduce consumption, and prevent environmental pollution, protect ecology, and improve the capacity to cope with climate change and disaster prevention and mitigation;
(4) those that can improve people's livelihood and public health levels;
(5) those that can promote modern agriculture or rural economic development; and
(6) those that can accelerate the socio-economic development of ethnic minority areas, remote areas, and impoverished areas.

Article 16 The holder of scientific and technological achievements may adopt the following methods to transform scientific and technological achievements:
(1) investing on its own to implement the transformation;
(2) transferring the scientific and technological achievements to others;
(3) licensing others to use the scientific and technological achievements;
(4) taking the scientific and technological achievements as cooperation conditions and jointly implementing the transformation with others;
(5) contributing the scientific and technological achievements as investment, converted into shares or capital contribution ratios; and
(6) other methods determined through consultation.
